{"id":"leetcode-1619","version":1,"status":"approved","title":"Mean of Array After Removing Some Elements","summary":"Given an integer array, calculate the mean of the elements excluding the smallest 5% and the largest 5%.","statement":"Given an integer array, calculate the mean of the elements excluding the smallest 5% and the largest 5%. Results within 0.00001 of the true mean are acceptable.","constraints":["Array length is 20–1,000 and divisible by 20; values are 0–100,000.","Remove exactly the smallest 5% and largest 5%, then return the mean of the remaining values."],"topics":["arrays","sorting"],"prerequisites":[],"signature":{"name":"trimmed_array_mean","parameters":[{"name":"arr","annotation":"list[int]","adapter":"raw","source_parameter":null}],"returns":"float","return_adapter":"raw","node_policy":"values","result_mode":"return","mutated_parameter":null,"immutable_parameters":[]},"starter_code":"def trimmed_array_mean(arr: list[int]) -> float:\n    # Write your solution here.\n    pass\n","reference_solution":"def trimmed_array_mean(arr):\n ordered=sorted(arr);cut=len(ordered)//20;kept=ordered[cut:len(ordered)-cut]\n return sum(kept)/len(kept)\n","brute_force_solution":null,"known_wrong_solutions":["def trimmed_array_mean(arr):\n ordered=sorted(arr);cut=0;kept=ordered[cut:len(ordered)-cut]\n return sum(kept)/len(kept)\n","def trimmed_array_mean(arr):\n ordered=sorted(arr);cut=len(ordered)//20;kept=ordered[cut:len(ordered)-cut-1]\n return sum(kept)/len(kept)\n"],"target_time_complexity":"O(n log n)","target_space_complexity":"O(n)","estimated_minutes":20,"rubric":{"algorithmic_insight":1,"prerequisites":1,"implementation":1,"performance_pressure":0,"edge_cases":0},"hints":["Sorting places both fixed-size tails at the ends.","Compute five percent as n//20 and average the middle slice.","Sort, slice from cut through n-cut, and divide its sum by its length.","Exactly cut values lie in each removed tail; every remaining index belongs to the required middle mul